1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,199
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,199 --> 00:00:05,160
I'm Peppa Pig. Snort.

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,920
This is
my little brother George.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:07,920
Oink, oink.

5
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,280
This is Mummy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,040
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,280
[SNORTS]

8
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig. Snort.

9
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:20,240
[♪♪♪]

10
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,439
PEPPA:
"Cleaning the Car."

11
00:00:23,439 --> 00:00:25,959
[GIGGLING]

12
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:29,520
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig is taking the family
for a drive in the country.

13
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:32,080
Come on. Snort.
Is everybody ready?

14
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,559
Hee-hee-hee.
Ready!

15
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:34,720
Oink, oink.

16
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,280
Yes, Daddy Pig,
we're ready.

17
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,280
But the car
isn't ready.

18
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:42,839
Snort.
Look how messy it is.

19
00:00:42,839 --> 00:00:44,960
Oh, it's not too bad.

20
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:47,599
You should see how messy it is
inside. Hee-hee-hee.

21
00:00:47,599 --> 00:00:49,120
[GASPS]

22
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,440
Naughty, messy Daddy.

23
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,720
Hee-hee-hee.
Naughty, messy Daddy.

24
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:56,640
[GIGGLES]

25
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,480
Look at all this rubbish.

26
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,879
Newspapers?

27
00:00:59,879 --> 00:01:01,599
Snort. They're mine.

28
00:01:01,599 --> 00:01:02,760
Sweets?

29
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:04,239
Snort.
They're mine.

30
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:06,000
Mr. Dinosaur?

31
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,160
Dine-saur. Grr!

32
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,640
Snort. We must clean the car
before we go for a drive.

33
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,600
Oh, right you are,
Mummy Pig.

34
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,320
Mummy, can we help
to clean the car?

35
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,320
Oink, oink.

36
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,399
Yes, if you want to.

37
00:01:19,399 --> 00:01:21,119
Hooray!

38
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,679
Daddy Pig has some warm
soapy water to wash the car.

39
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,720
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho.

40
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,720
Daddy Pig is washing the roof.

41
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,000
[SNORTS]

42
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,960
Mummy Pig
is washing the bonnet.

43
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,320
[SNORTS]

44
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:37,800
Peppa is washing the doors.

45
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,039
Snort. Snort.
Hee-hee-hee.

46
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:42,399
George wants
to wash the windows,

47
00:01:42,399 --> 00:01:44,399
but he is too little.

48
00:01:44,399 --> 00:01:45,800
[CRIES]

49
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:50,520
Snort. Poor George.
Let me help you.

50
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,440
[GIGGLING]

51
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,000
[ALL LAUGH]

52
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,559
Oh, dear.

53
00:01:55,559 --> 00:02:00,080
George has dropped his sponge
in a muddy puddle.

54
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,679
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

55
00:02:01,679 --> 00:02:03,119
PEPPA:
George.

56
00:02:03,119 --> 00:02:05,440
You're making the car
all muddy again.

57
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,600
Oink.

58
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,479
[GIGGLES]

59
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:12,160
I will wash the mud off.

60
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,880
Peppa, don't use the--

61
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,079
Muddy water.

62
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,640
Oh, dear.

63
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:22,880
Peppa has thrown the muddy
water all over the car.

64
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,120
Oh.

65
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,680
Snort.
Never mind.

66
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,160
We can use the garden hose
to clean it off.

67
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:31,200
Yes, yes! Snort.
Can I hold the hose?

68
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,840
[GIGGLES]

69
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,160
Ha-ha-ha-ha.
Snort. Snort.

70
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,600
[GIGGLES]

71
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,359
Peppa holds the hose

72
00:02:40,359 --> 00:02:44,200
and Daddy Pig
turns on the water.

73
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:47,280
Snort. Where's the water?

74
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:50,079
[GURGLES]

75
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:52,400
Whaaa!

76
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,840
[GIGGLES]

77
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,239
Oh! Peppa, stop.

78
00:02:56,239 --> 00:02:57,880
Sorry, Mummy.

79
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:00,560
[GIGGLES]

80
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,799
Oh.

81
00:03:01,799 --> 00:03:03,120
Ah!

82
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,239
Daddy Pig, please
turn off the water.

83
00:03:06,239 --> 00:03:08,440
Oh. Ha-ha-ha-ha.

84
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,519
No need to panic.

85
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,600
Oh, dear, everyone is wet.

86
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,720
Ho-ho-ho. At least
the car has been washed.

87
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,959
We've all been washed.

88
00:03:19,959 --> 00:03:21,720
[ALL LAUGH]

89
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:24,720
You go and dry yourselves
while I polish the car.

90
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,160
See you later.

91
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,480
See you later. Snort.

92
00:03:35,239 --> 00:03:37,600
Daddy Pig
is polishing the car so well

93
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:41,040
he can see his face in it.

94
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,160
[SNORTS, LAUGHS]

95
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:45,200
What a funny face.

96
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,200
Phbbt.

97
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,600
Oh, more funny faces.

98
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,280
It's Peppa and George.

99
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,399
Oh, ha-ha.

100
00:03:51,399 --> 00:03:52,880
And Mummy Pig.

101
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:55,440
What a lovely
shiny car.

102
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,480
Yes, I am a bit
of an expert

103
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:58,959
at these things.

104
00:03:58,959 --> 00:04:00,399
[ALL LAUGH]

105
00:04:00,399 --> 00:04:03,040
Snort.
Come on, I'll drive today.

106
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,119
Is everybody ready?

107
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:06,040
MUMMY, GEORGE, PEPPA:
Ready.

108
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,679
Then let's go.

109
00:04:08,679 --> 00:04:10,760
[HORN BEEPS]

110
00:04:14,519 --> 00:04:17,240
Snort. I hope you will all
keep this car clean today.

111
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,599
Yes, Mummy Pig.

112
00:04:18,599 --> 00:04:20,000
Yes, Mummy Pig.

113
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,200
Oink, oink.

114
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,200
Oh!
Whoa!
Aah!

115
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,000
[GIGGLES]

116
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,280
Mummy, now you've made
the car all muddy again.

117
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,800
Ha-ha.
Naughty Mummy.

118
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,880
Hee-hee.
Naughty, messy Mummy.

119
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,360
[ALL LAUGH]

120
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,840
[ALL LAUGHING, SNORTING]

121
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,479
[HORN BEEPS]

122
00:04:51,479 --> 00:04:53,520
PEPPA:
"Lunch."

123
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,400
Peppa and George have come

124
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:58,919
to Granny Pig and Grandpa Pig's
house for lunch.

125
00:04:58,919 --> 00:05:01,200
Hee-hee-hee. Snort.
Granny Pig.

126
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,320
Oink. Ganggy Ig.
Hee-hee-hee.

127
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,520
Hello, my little ones.

128
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:07,800
Snort. Would you like
to pick some vegetables

129
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,440
from the garden for lunch?

130
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,400
Yes, please.
Oink.

131
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,599
[GIGGLING]

132
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,120
Grandpa Pig.

133
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,280
Baba Ig.

134
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:20,960
Snort.
Hello, Peppa, George.

135
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,120
This is Grandpa Pig's
vegetable garden.

136
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:26,000
He has grown
all these vegetables himself.

137
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,880
Grrr.

138
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,520
GRANDPA:
What's this?

139
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,719
Dine-saur.

140
00:05:31,719 --> 00:05:34,640
A dinosaur? Ho-ho-ho-ho.

141
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,039
Snort. Let's choose
some vegetables for lunch.

142
00:05:38,039 --> 00:05:40,120
[GIGGLES]

143
00:05:42,039 --> 00:05:44,840
Peppa,
do you like tomatoes?

144
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,960
Snort. Yes, Grandpa Pig.

145
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:49,919
George, do you like tomatoes?

146
00:05:49,919 --> 00:05:51,440
No.

147
00:05:52,719 --> 00:05:55,400
George
does not like tomatoes.

148
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,320
Oh, dear.

149
00:06:00,479 --> 00:06:02,599
Do you both like lettuce?

150
00:06:02,599 --> 00:06:04,719
Snort. Yes, Grandpa Pig.

151
00:06:04,719 --> 00:06:06,080
No.

152
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:09,159
Snort. George does not
like lettuce.

153
00:06:09,159 --> 00:06:10,359
Oh, dear.

154
00:06:10,359 --> 00:06:13,520
I must have something
that George likes.

155
00:06:14,919 --> 00:06:16,760
Do you like cucumber?

156
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:18,359
Yuck.

157
00:06:18,359 --> 00:06:20,200
George does not like cucumbers

158
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,599
and he does not like lettuce
and he does not like tomatoes.

159
00:06:23,599 --> 00:06:27,479
Well, George,
what vegetable do you like?

160
00:06:27,479 --> 00:06:29,440
Chocolate cake.

161
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,599
Hee-hee-hee.
Silly George.

162
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:35,080
Chocolate cake
isn't a vegetable.

163
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,200
Ho ho ho. Snort.

164
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,159
Maybe George
will like the vegetables

165
00:06:38,159 --> 00:06:40,640
when they're made
into a lovely salad.

166
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,479
[GIGGLES]

167
00:06:43,479 --> 00:06:48,479
Ohh, lovely fresh tomatoes,
lettuce and cucumber.

168
00:06:48,479 --> 00:06:51,440
Snort.
First we have to wash them.

169
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:54,799
Peppa and George help
Granny Pig wash the vegetables.

170
00:06:54,799 --> 00:06:58,080
[BOTH GIGGLE]

171
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,120
[LAUGHS]

172
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:03,159
Ha-ha-ha-ha. Snort.
Maybe that's enough washing.

173
00:07:05,799 --> 00:07:07,760
Granny Pig
has made the tomatoes,

174
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,159
lettuce and cucumber
into a salad.

175
00:07:10,159 --> 00:07:13,599
Grandpa Pig, can you
call everyone to lunch?

176
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,840
Lunch!

177
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:17,520
[BOTH GIGGLE]

178
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:20,039
Granny Pig has made pizza
for lunch.

179
00:07:20,039 --> 00:07:22,000
And here's some salad made

180
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,320
with Grandpa's tomatoes,
lettuce and cucumber.

181
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,359
Tuck in, everyone.

182
00:07:28,359 --> 00:07:31,359
[GOBBLING AND GRUNTING]

183
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,479
George has eaten his pizza,

184
00:07:38,479 --> 00:07:40,680
but George does not like
the tomatoes

185
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,159
or the lettuce
or the cucumber.

186
00:07:43,159 --> 00:07:47,159
Oh, dear, George.
Don't you like the salad?

187
00:07:47,159 --> 00:07:48,239
No.

188
00:07:48,239 --> 00:07:51,000
George,
just try a little bit

189
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,760
of this lovely tomato.

190
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,880
Yuck.

191
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,840
George, this is cucumber.

192
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,799
Grandpa Pig grew it
in his garden.

193
00:07:59,799 --> 00:08:01,320
Bleah.

194
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,599
Try a piece of lettuce, George.

195
00:08:03,599 --> 00:08:05,200
It's yummy.

196
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:08,640
[CRYING]

197
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,760
Now, now, George.

198
00:08:12,479 --> 00:08:15,159
Look what I'm doing.

199
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,719
Now it's a dinosaur.

200
00:08:19,719 --> 00:08:21,520
Oink. Dine-saur.

201
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:24,599
Hee-hee-hee. Grrr.

202
00:08:24,599 --> 00:08:27,120
George loves dinosaurs.

203
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:31,200
George is eating the tomatoes,
lettuce and cucumber.

204
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:33,120
Well done, George.

205
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,919
Oink.

206
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:36,959
Would you like some more,
George?

207
00:08:36,959 --> 00:08:38,400
Full.

208
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,280
George, are you too full

209
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:44,439
to eat any more tomatoes,
lettuce or cucumber?

210
00:08:44,439 --> 00:08:45,680
Oink.

211
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:48,560
George is too full
to eat any more.

212
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,439
George, are you too full
to eat anything more?

213
00:08:51,439 --> 00:08:52,800
Oink, oink.

214
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,959
George is too full
to eat anything more.

215
00:08:54,959 --> 00:09:00,079
Oh, well, then you won't want
any of this chocolate cake.

216
00:09:00,079 --> 00:09:02,199
Chocolate cake.

217
00:09:02,199 --> 00:09:06,000
Oink, oink. Hee-hee-hee.

218
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,079
GRANDPA PIG:
My word.

219
00:09:08,079 --> 00:09:11,079
George seems to have got
his appetite back.

220
00:09:11,079 --> 00:09:14,319
[LAUGHING]
[LAUGHING]

221
00:09:14,319 --> 00:09:16,880
[GIGGLES]

222
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:20,880
PEPPA:
"Camping."

223
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:23,280
Peppa and her family
are going camping.

224
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,199
I love camping.

225
00:09:25,199 --> 00:09:26,720
[SNORTS]

226
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,600
We're here.

227
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,640
PEPPA, GEORGE, MUMMY:
Hooray!

228
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,839
[GIGGLING]

229
00:09:32,839 --> 00:09:36,640
Peppa, George,
this is the tent I had

230
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,839
when I was a little boy.

231
00:09:38,839 --> 00:09:42,360
Daddy, how are you gonna
make that into a tent?

232
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,280
DADDY PIG:
Don't worry, Peppa.

233
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,760
I'm an expert at camping.
Snort.

234
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:50,040
Mummy Pig, put the tent
on the poles, please.

235
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,480
That's it.

236
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,120
Easy as pie.

237
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,240
Oh.

238
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,880
Do these pegs do anything?

239
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,240
Of course.

240
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:59,839
I forgot
about the pegs.

241
00:09:59,839 --> 00:10:03,160
The pegs hold the tent up.

242
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,560
There.

243
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:07,160
Snort. The tent
is a bit little.

244
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,760
It was big enough for me
when I was a boy,

245
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:11,959
but it does look
a bit small now.

246
00:10:11,959 --> 00:10:13,959
That's because
you've grown a bit

247
00:10:13,959 --> 00:10:15,880
since you were a boy,
Daddy Pig.

248
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:19,400
And your tummy has grown
the most of all. Hee-hee.

249
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:23,720
Ho-ho-ho. Talking of tummies,
we should cook supper.

250
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,160
Yes, yes.

251
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:28,319
First we have to collect sticks
to make a fire.

252
00:10:28,319 --> 00:10:29,319
Yipee!

253
00:10:29,319 --> 00:10:31,000
Peppa and George

254
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,560
are helping Daddy Pig collect
sticks for the campfire.

255
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:36,560
George, I'll pick up the sticks,
and you can carry them.

256
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:38,040
Oink, oink.

257
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,240
[GIGGLING]

258
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,480
[GIGGLES]

259
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,800
Collecting sticks is fun.

260
00:10:44,959 --> 00:10:47,240
Good.
That's enough sticks.

261
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:52,000
That's a splendid campfire.

262
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,800
Snort. Now I'll light it.

263
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,439
Here are the matches.

264
00:10:55,439 --> 00:10:58,120
Ho-ho, we don't need matches.

265
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,400
Daddy, how can you light it
without matches?

266
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,880
I'm going to make fire
the old way,

267
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,520
by simply rubbing
these two sticks together.

268
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:08,040
Daddy Pig is rubbing
the two sticks together

269
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:11,600
to light the campfire.

270
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,719
Where is the fire,
Daddy?

271
00:11:13,719 --> 00:11:15,680
Nearly there.

272
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:17,400
[BLOWS]

273
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,280
Hooray!
[WHEEZES]

274
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,680
Easy as pie.

275
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,040
[ALL LAUGH]

276
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:25,319
Snort. Now we can heat up
the tomato soup.

277
00:11:25,319 --> 00:11:29,040
Ahh, listen
to the sounds of nature.

278
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,280
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

279
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,079
What is that sound?

280
00:11:32,079 --> 00:11:34,520
That is the sound
of crickets chirping.

281
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,120
[OWL HOOTS]

282
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,520
What is that?

283
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:39,000
That's an owl.

284
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,040
Look, there it is.

285
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,319
[HOOTS]

286
00:11:42,319 --> 00:11:43,719
Wow.
Ohh.

287
00:11:43,719 --> 00:11:45,319
[GURGLING NOISE]

288
00:11:45,319 --> 00:11:47,520
And what's that noise?

289
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,959
Oh, I'm not sure.

290
00:11:48,959 --> 00:11:50,560
[GURGLES]

291
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,319
It's Daddy's tummy.

292
00:11:52,319 --> 00:11:54,199
[ALL LAUGH]

293
00:11:54,199 --> 00:11:57,400
My tummy rumbling is one
of the best sounds of nature.

294
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,959
It means it's time to eat.
Snort.

295
00:11:59,959 --> 00:12:02,240
I love tomato soup.

296
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,719
So do I.

297
00:12:03,719 --> 00:12:05,839
[SLURPING]

298
00:12:05,839 --> 00:12:07,680
Oh, there's another one
of Daddy Pig's

299
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,319
sounds of nature.

300
00:12:09,319 --> 00:12:10,560
[BURPS]

301
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,800
Eh? What?

302
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:12,920
[ALL LAUGH]

303
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:15,040
Come on, children,
into the tent.

304
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,319
It's bedtime.

305
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:19,920
We won't all fit in.
The tent is too little.

306
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:23,199
It will be fine.
In you go.

307
00:12:23,199 --> 00:12:27,920
Snort. Move further in,
Mummy Pig.

308
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:30,920
PEPPA:
Daddy, you're too big
for the tent.

309
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,760
Snort. Never mind.

310
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,839
I'd rather sleep
outside anyway.

311
00:12:34,839 --> 00:12:36,160
Good night, Daddy Pig.

312
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,360
Good night,
Daddy.

313
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,520
Night. Night.

314
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:40,000
Good night, everyone.

315
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,800
Mummy Pig, Peppa and George

316
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,560
are sleeping in the tent.

317
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:46,199
Daddy Pig is sleeping outside,
under the stars.

318
00:12:46,199 --> 00:12:48,959
Ahh. I love camping.

319
00:12:48,959 --> 00:12:52,839
Sleeping in the open air
with the stars above me.

320
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:57,640
Maybe this wasn't such
a good idea after all.

321
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:00,040
Brr.

322
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,599
[ROOSTER CROWS]

323
00:13:01,599 --> 00:13:03,120
It is morning.

324
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:07,040
Daddy, it was lovely and cozy
in the tent.

325
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:09,000
Oh, where's Daddy?

326
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,839
Daddy Pig has gone.

327
00:13:10,839 --> 00:13:14,439
Poor Daddy Pig.
He must have been cold and wet.

328
00:13:14,439 --> 00:13:16,079
And now where is he?

329
00:13:16,079 --> 00:13:18,079
[SNORING]

330
00:13:18,079 --> 00:13:19,719
What's that sound?

331
00:13:19,719 --> 00:13:22,160
It sounds like snoring.

332
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:25,040
[PEPPA AND GEORGE GIGGLING]

333
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,880
[SNORING]

334
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,920
Hee-hee-hee.
Daddy Pig.

335
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:30,160
What?

336
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:31,319
Daddy, you're safe.

337
00:13:31,319 --> 00:13:34,160
Ho-ho.
Of course I'm safe.

338
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,800
Snort.
I'm an expert at camping.

339
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,920
I slept in the car.

340
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,079
Hee-hee. Silly Daddy.

341
00:13:41,079 --> 00:13:43,680
Ho-ho.
I love camping.

342
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,760
[ALL LAUGHING]

343
00:13:50,319 --> 00:13:52,400
[♪♪♪]

344
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:55,120
PEPPA:
"The Sleepy Princess."

345
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,160
It is night time.

346
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,760
Peppa and George
are going to bed.

347
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,839
[GIGGLING]

348
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,680
Good night,
Peppa and George. Snort.

349
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,640
Mummy? Daddy?

350
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,800
Yes, Peppa?

351
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:12,719
I'm not sleepy.
Can I have a story?

352
00:14:12,719 --> 00:14:15,400
But maybe George is sleepy
and doesn't want a story.

353
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,839
George, do you want a story?

354
00:14:17,839 --> 00:14:19,680
[SOFTLY]
Say yes.

355
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,040
Oink, oink.

356
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,760
Ho-ho-ho. Snort.
All right.

357
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:25,640
I will tell you
just one story.

358
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:28,000
Snort. If Daddy Pig
tells you a story,

359
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
you must both promise
to go to sleep.

360
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
We promise. Snort.

361
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,479
Oink, oink.

362
00:14:34,479 --> 00:14:37,479
Hm. I think
I'll tell you the story

363
00:14:37,479 --> 00:14:40,240
of "The Sleepy Princess."

364
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:44,240
Is it a good story?
It sounds a bit boring.

365
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,520
It's not boring.
It's very good.

366
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:50,479
Is there a little princess
in it?

367
00:14:50,479 --> 00:14:54,319
Peppa, if you keep talking,
Daddy Pig can't start the story.

368
00:14:54,319 --> 00:14:55,760
Sorry, Mummy.

369
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:59,120
Is there a little princess
in the story, Daddy?

370
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,280
Ho-ho.

371
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:03,920
Yes, there is
a little princess in it.

372
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,439
[SNORTS]

373
00:15:05,439 --> 00:15:06,560
Oink, oink.

374
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:09,880
Hm. "The Sleepy Princess."

375
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:14,000
[♪♪♪]

376
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,079
DADDY PIG:
Once upon a time in a castle,

377
00:15:17,079 --> 00:15:19,520
there lived
a little princess,

378
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:23,160
and she was called
the Sleepy Princess.

379
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:26,040
Daddy,
why was she called that?

380
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,439
I'll get to that later.

381
00:15:27,439 --> 00:15:30,000
Was the Sleepy Princess
pretty?

382
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,079
Yes, she was very pretty.

383
00:15:32,079 --> 00:15:35,319
She loved looking at herself
in the mirror.

384
00:15:35,319 --> 00:15:39,240
I am so pretty. Snort.
Hee-hee-hee-hee.

385
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,839
Who else was living
in the castle?

386
00:15:41,839 --> 00:15:43,240
Uh, well...

387
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,439
The others
in the castle were

388
00:15:45,439 --> 00:15:46,880
the Small Prince...

389
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:47,839
Oink, oink.

390
00:15:47,839 --> 00:15:49,839
Queen Mummy...
Snort.

391
00:15:49,839 --> 00:15:52,319
...and King Daddy.
Snort.

392
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:55,199
That's right. They were
all living there as well.

393
00:15:55,199 --> 00:15:57,359
PEPPA:
Did King Daddy
have a big tummy?

394
00:15:57,359 --> 00:16:00,640
Of course not.
He was very handsome.

395
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,000
Like me. Snort.

396
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,560
[GIGGLE]

397
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,800
Anyway,
there was also a dragon.

398
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,160
Dine-saur!

399
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:09,479
A dinosaur?

400
00:16:09,479 --> 00:16:13,520
Oh, yes, it wasn't a dragon,
it was a dinosaur.

401
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:18,839
Living outside
was a huge fierce dinosaur.

402
00:16:18,839 --> 00:16:22,240
Rawrrr! Rawrr-arr.

403
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:24,800
Rrawrrr!

404
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,439
[CRYING]
Oh, dear.

405
00:16:27,439 --> 00:16:31,839
Maybe the dinosaur wasn't
quite that fierce, Daddy Pig?

406
00:16:31,839 --> 00:16:33,079
Sorry, George.

407
00:16:33,079 --> 00:16:36,880
No, the dinosaur
was very gentle.

408
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:39,479
It ate lots of grass.

409
00:16:39,479 --> 00:16:41,400
[CRUNCHES]

410
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,599
[BURPS]

411
00:16:42,599 --> 00:16:43,839
[BURPS]

412
00:16:43,839 --> 00:16:44,880
Daddy Pig.

413
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,000
Oop, sorry.

414
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,760
I was being the dinosaur.

415
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:49,319
[LAUGHS]
[GIGGLING]

416
00:16:49,319 --> 00:16:50,959
Hee-hee-hee.

417
00:16:50,959 --> 00:16:55,400
Daddy, why is the princess
called the Sleepy Princess?

418
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:57,000
I'm coming to that.

419
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
You see, the sun set,

420
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,680
then the stars and moon
came out,

421
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:04,639
and everyone got very sleepy.

422
00:17:04,639 --> 00:17:07,159
[YAWNS]

423
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:08,960
[YAWNS]

424
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,800
[YAWNS]
[YAWNS]

425
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:16,399
But the most sleepy of all
was the Sleepy Princess.

426
00:17:16,399 --> 00:17:18,159
[YAWNS]

427
00:17:18,159 --> 00:17:20,159
[YAWNS]

428
00:17:20,159 --> 00:17:22,079
Peppa, are you sleepy?

429
00:17:22,079 --> 00:17:25,680
Snort. No, Daddy.
I am not sleepy at all.

430
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:28,840
[SNORING]

431
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,600
MUMMY PIG:
But somebody is.

432
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,000
George, wake up.

433
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,080
You'll miss the end
of the story.

434
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,360
Oink.

435
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,399
DADDY PIG:
Well, Peppa
might not be sleepy,

436
00:17:38,399 --> 00:17:40,720
but the Sleepy Princess
certainly was.

437
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:43,040
Looking at herself all day
in the mirror

438
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,399
had completely worn her out.

439
00:17:45,399 --> 00:17:46,760
[YAWNS]

440
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,720
Let's carry you to bed.
Snort.

441
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,680
Good night.
[SNORING]

442
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:57,760
The Sleepy Princess
was so sleepy,

443
00:17:57,760 --> 00:18:01,360
she had fallen fast asleep.

444
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:06,000
[SNORING]

445
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,600
[SOFTLY]
Thank you for that story,
King Daddy.

446
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,200
[SOFTLY]
You're welcome,
Queen Mummy.

447
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:15,280
And our little prince
and princess enjoyed it too.

448
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:17,520
[SNORING, WHISTLING]

449
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,159
[♪♪♪]

450
00:18:22,159 --> 00:18:23,960
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

451
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:27,040
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

452
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,520
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

453
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:29,560
GEORGE:
Oink, oink.

454
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:30,639
[BOTH GIGGLE]

455
00:18:30,639 --> 00:18:32,960
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

456
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,600
[SNORTS]

